    definition: "Pushing risk, cost, or harm onto other teams, communities, or the future so metrics look clean. Externalization shows up as pollution, shadow labor, or brittle dependencies that live outside audits. Ethotechnics counters it with oversight horizons, MPIs, and transparent repair logs.",
